initely  a bit disappointing  and i guess if you think about it apple  would rather upsell their much more  expensive 16 inch macbook pro  to the people who really care about  display size because it's already been  working  in recent years and then if we dig a  little bit deeper  a 15 inch macbook air for 15 or 1600  dollars  would end up costing more than their  base 13 inch macbook pro for  1300 which wouldn't really make sense  because the pro line should logically be  more expensive  so because of those reasons i don't  think we'll be seeing a 15 inch air  anytime soon  but the totally redesigned 13-inch air  is definitely coming  and i think we figured out when apple is  going to release it  because of how groundbreaking the  current m1 macbook air already is  apple totally doesn't have to update it  until  2022 just like the rumors are pointing  to  in fact i personally believe that we  won't be seeing a new macbook air  until it gets a brand new m2 chip  built on tsmc's three nanometer  architecture  because right now they're still stuck  with the five nanometer  so even if they make a new chip it's not  really going to be any more efficient  which is what matters the most for the  macbook air and as of right now  tsmc is expected to have the three  nanometer chips ready  in the fall of 2022 and that's when i  think  the fully redesigned macbook air with  the m2 is coming  and if you think that's way too long of  a wait we believe that apple is going to  be focusing more on the pro machines  until then like for example the fully  redesigned 14  and 16 inch macbook pros coming around  this summer  with the m1x chip and then the m1x or  m1z  redesigned imax coming in the fall or  maybe even the winter  and then next year in 2022 we're finally  going to be getting the redesigned  macbook air  and a redesigned base 1300 macbook pro  with an m2 chip which will be weaker  but more efficient than the m1x on the  higher end models  of course until they come out with the  m2x chip so that's basically my personal  speculations for the macbook release  timeline  and now i want to finish off by  answering one  final question should you wait for the  redesigned macbook air  well if you know that you're not willing  to wait over a full year  to end up paying a higher 1300 price  for the redesigned macbook air then i  would honestly just buy the current  m1 air right now for a thousand dollars  and enjoy it for all of those months  that you could have ended up waiting  or if you want some extra power then i  would simply wait for the m1x 14-inch  macbook pro  coming most likely sometime this summer  but keep in mind  that it's likely going to be priced at  around 1800 to 2  000 so if you're not willing to pay for  that  then seriously just buy the m1 macbook  air right now  because it's an absolutely killer value  so hopefully you enjoyed this video and  if you did  check out our macbook air review right  over there and click that circle above  to subscribe for more videos like this  one  thanks for watching and we'll see you in  the next video  [Music]
 

